
                    DayDream BBS V1.00, Conferences.DAT
                    -----------------------------------

OFFSET  TYPE     LENGTH  DESCRIPTION                                     FLAGS
==============================================================================
 0000   BYTE       01    NUMBER OF THE CONFERENCE                          (-)
 0001   STRING     39    CONFERENCE NAME                                   (-)
 0041   STRING     39    CONFERENCE BASE PATH                              (-)
 0081   BYTE       01    NUMBER OF FILE AREAS IN CONFERENCE                (-)
 0082   BYTE       01    NUMBER OF FILE AREA TO PLACE UPLOADS IN (0=DSBLD) (-)
 0083   BYTE       01    NUMBER OF MESSAGE BASES IN CONFERENCE             (-)
 0084   BYTE       01    NUMBER OF MESSAGE BASE TO PLACE COMMENTS IN       (-)
 0085   BYTE       01    --- --- ---                                       (-)
 0086   WORD       02    CONFERENCE FLAGS (SEE BELOW)                      (-)
 0088   STRING     49    PATH OF DIRECTORY TO PLACE UPLOADS IN             (-)
 0138   STRING     29    AREALIST FOR GLOBAL SCAN                          (-)
 0168	STRING     15    CONFERENCE PASSWORD                               (-)
 0184	FREE BLOCK 116   FREE SPACE RESERVED FOR FUTURE DEVELOPMENT        (-)
 0300   STRUCTURE  200   FIRST MESSAGE BASE STRUCTURE (SEE BELOW)          (S)

   ... CONTINUES WITH AS MANY MESSAGE BASE STRUCTURES AS CONFERENCE HAS ...
  .... THEN COMES THE VERY NEXT CONFERENCE, UNTIL ALL CONFS ARE WRITTEN ....

==============================================================================

                          Message Base Structure
                          ----------------------

OFFSET  TYPE     LENGTH  DESCRIPTION                                     FLAGS
==============================================================================
 0000   BYTE       01    MESSAGE BASE FLAGS (SEE BELOW)                    (-)
 0001   BYTE       01    NUMBER OF MESSAGE BASE                            (-)
 0002   WORD       02    LOWEST MESSAGE IN THIS AREA                       (-)
 0004   WORD       02    HIGHEST MESSAGE IN THIS AREA                      (-)
 0006   WORD       02    MAXIMUM AMOUNT OF MESSAGES ALLOWED                (-)
 0008   STRING     20    NAME OF THE MESSAGE BASE                          (-)
 0029   FREE BLOCK 08    FREE SPACE RESERVED FOR FUTURE DEVELOPMENT  !!!   (-)
 0037   STRING     25    FIDONET: MESSAGE AREA TAG NAME                    (-)
 0063   STRING     57    FIDONET: ORIGIN LINE FOR THIS AREA                (-)
 0121   BYTE       01    FIDONET: OPTIONS                                  (-)
 0122   WORD       02    FIDONET: ZONE                                     (-)
 0124   WORD       02    FIDONET: NET ID                                   (-)
 0126   WORD       02    FIDONET: NODE                                     (-)
 0128   WORD       02    FIDONET: POINT                                    (-)
 0130   BYTE       01    ACCESS LEVEL REQUIRED TO READ THIS MSG BASE       (-)
 0131   BYTE       01    ACCESS LEVEL REQUIRED TO POST TO THIS MSG BASE    (-)
 0132   FREE BLOCK 68    FREE SPACE RESERVED FOR FUTURE DEVELOPMENT        (-)
 0200   END        00    END OF MESSAGE BASE STRUCTURE                     (-)
==============================================================================


BIT   MEANING WHEN SET AS PRESENTED BELOW                     CONFERENCE FLAGS
==============================================================================
000   FREE-DOWNLOAD ON ALL FILES IN THIS CONFERENCE
001   NO FILE OR BYTE CREDITS FOR UPLOADING
002   DISABLE SENT-BY LINES
003   18 CHARACTERS LONG FILENAMES
004   ASK DESTINATION FILE AREA
005   DO NOT ALLOW WILDCARDS IN FILENAMES (UPLOAD)
006   DO NOT ALLOW WILDCARD FILEFLAGGING
007   NO DUPECHECK (SKIP THIS CONF IN GLOBAL DUPE CHECK)
008   NO FILECHECK
009   NO REQUESTERS
010   PRIVATE FLAG -- DO NOT USE
 :
 :
 ·
 .
015
==============================================================================


BIT   MEANING WHEN SET AS PRESENTED BELOW                   MESSAGE BASE FLAGS
==============================================================================
 0    0: ALLOW PUBLIC MESSAGES         1: DO NOT ALLOW PUBLIC MESSAGES
 1    0: ALLOW PRIVATE MESSAGES        1: DO NOT ALLOW PRIVATE MESSAGES
 2    0: MESSAGES USE REAL NAMES       1: MESSAGES USE HANDLES / ALIASES
 3    0: QUOTE LINE AFTER ACTUAL QUOTE 1: USE THE "> " QUOTING METHOD
 4    0: A PLAIN "> " WILL DO          1: INSERT INITIALS BEFORE THE "> "
 5    0: DO NOT ALLOW FILE ATTACHS     1: ALLOW FILE ATTACHS
 6    0: ALL = ALL                     1: ALL = EALL, BYTEJAMMER MODE
 7    PRIVATE FLAG -- DO NOT USE
==============================================================================

BIT   MEANING WHEN SET AS PRESENTED BELOW                      FIDONET OPTIONS
==============================================================================
 0    0: LOCAL MESSAGE BASE            1: ECHOMAIL OR NETMAIL AREA
 1    0: ECHOMAIL AREA (IF BIT 0 SET)  1: NETMAIL AREA (IF BIT 0 SET)
 .
 .
 7
